From c91d771b97a80be93599f8cc4674fd64fd946409 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Chiro <chiro2001@163.com>
Date: Sun, 13 Sep 2026 16:39:40 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 270/274] feat(execution): add opt-in AOCL int8 exact-blocked
 provider

Add vendor:aocl-lpgemm-int8-exact-blocked, a second executor of the pinned
aocl_gemm_s8s8s32os32 path that splits K into
Kc = min(2048, floor(2**24 / (max_abs_a * max_abs_b))) chunks so every f32
round trip inside the kernel operates on an integer partial sum bounded by
2**24 and is therefore the identity. Per-chunk int32 outputs are accumulated
with Python arbitrary-precision integers and range-checked against int32, so
the result equals the contract's exact int32 sum for every accepted K
(K <= 133144), independent of the kernel's internal reduction order.

The entry declares numeric_class=exact and a proven exact_contract_bound
envelope (deviation_bound_by_k = 0) with the Kc rule, proof obligation and
checkable residual assumptions/withdrawal path. It is opt-in only: not in
default_providers, skipped by the resolver unless
numeric.require_proven_deviation_bound / provider.mode=required / an explicit
declared fallback chain opts in, and not added to OpDefinition.allowed_providers
so the frozen contract digest and default plan digest stay byte-identical to
393d28e0f.

Evidence: tree-vs-tree zero-default matrix (identical modulo label), differential
matrix max deviation 0 over K in {1024,1040,1041,2048,2049,16696,133144} with
all-127/mixed/random, threads 1/2/6 bitwise identical, Kc-bypass and ERR-0010
counterexample controls; rule 8 focused 105 passed and full 2098 passed,
7 skipped.

(cherry picked from commit 63980fc5e9e31895b2621d1fb1b38ac39638e6df)
